problem:
Problem description
- This is a single-period assignment-and-setup planning problem with a set of parts $$\mathcal{P}$$ and a set of candidate machines $$\mathcal{M}$$.
- Each part $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ has required quantity $$q_p$$ and must be processed exactly once on one machine.
- The unit processing cost of assigning part $$p$$ to machine $$m$$ is $$c_{pm}$$.
- Each machine $$m \in \mathcal{M}$$ has a fixed setup cost $$f_m$$ that is incurred once if the machine is used for at least one part.
- Three machines are distinguished as $$m_A$$, $$m_B$$, and $$m_C$$.
- Five parts are distinguished as $$p^{(1)}$$, $$p^{(2)}$$, $$p^{(3)}$$, $$p^{(4)}$$, and $$p^{(5)}$$ for special routing restrictions.
- The planning goal is to minimize the total cost made up of all processing costs and all incurred setup costs.

- Required business constraints:
  - Every part demand must be fully satisfied.
  - Each part must be assigned to exactly one machine.
  - If $$p^{(1)}$$ is assigned to $$m_A$$, then $$p^{(2)}$$ must be assigned to either $$m_B$$ or $$m_C$$.
  - If $$p^{(1)}$$ is assigned to either $$m_B$$ or $$m_C$$, then $$p^{(2)}$$ must be assigned to $$m_A$$.
  - Part $$p^{(3)}$$ must be processed on $$m_A$$.
  - Part $$p^{(4)}$$ must be processed on $$m_B$$.
  - Part $$p^{(5)}$$ must be processed on $$m_C$$.
  - The total number of parts assigned to $$m_C$$ must not exceed the capacity limit $$U_C$$.
  - A machine becomes active if at least one part is assigned to it, and any active machine incurs its setup cost.

- A solution is represented by:
  - Binary assignment variables $$x_{pm}$$, where $$x_{pm} = 1$$ means part $$p$$ is assigned to machine $$m$$, and $$x_{pm} = 0$$ otherwise.
  - Binary activation variables $$y_m$$, where $$y_m = 1$$ means machine $$m$$ is used, and $$y_m = 0$$ otherwise.
  - The minimized total cost of processing plus machine setups.

Input Format
{
  "parts": {
    "count": "$$P$$",
    "indices": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$"
  },
  "machines": {
    "count": "$$M$$",
    "indices": "$$\\mathcal{M}$$"
  },
  "demand": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "meaning": "$$q_p$$ is the required quantity of part $$p$$"
  },
  "processing_cost": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times M$$",
    "meaning": "$$c_{pm}$$ is the unit processing cost of part $$p$$ on machine $$m$$"
  },
  "setup_cost": {
    "shape": "$$M$$",
    "meaning": "$$f_m$$ is the fixed setup cost of machine $$m$$ if it is used"
  },
  "distinguished_machines": {
    "A": "$$m_A$$",
    "B": "$$m_B$$",
    "C": "$$m_C$$"
  },
  "distinguished_parts": {
    "first": "$$p^{(1)}$$",
    "second": "$$p^{(2)}$$",
    "third": "$$p^{(3)}$$",
    "fourth": "$$p^{(4)}$$",
    "fifth": "$$p^{(5)}$$"
  },
  "routing_rules": {
    "meaning": "logical assignment dependencies involving $$p^{(1)}$$ and $$p^{(2)}$$"
  },
  "fixed_assignments": {
    "meaning": "parts with mandatory machine choices"
  },
  "capacity_limits": {
    "machine_C": "$$U_C$$",
    "meaning": "maximum number of parts allowed on $$m_C$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "assignment_matrix": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times M$$",
    "meaning": "$$x_{pm}$$ indicates whether part $$p$$ is assigned to machine $$m$$"
  },
  "machine_activation": {
    "shape": "$$M$$",
    "meaning": "$$y_m$$ indicates whether machine $$m$$ is activated"
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "meaning": "the minimized total cost"
  }
}

